{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8xOTk5LS1CZWZvcmUvQW4lMjBPZmZpY2VyJTIwQW5kJTIwQSUyMEdlbnRsZW1hbiUyMCUyODE5ODIlMjkv","type":"movie","name":"An Officer And A Gentleman","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/69adZbLeRk5TNQ3e0008dMnde9p.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/w1lWBgc1FWtS2EM0vksA6bZtRYw.jpg","description":"Zack Mayo is an aloof, taciturn man who aspires to be a navy pilot. Once he arrives at training camp for his 13-week officer's course, Mayo runs afoul of abrasive, no-nonsense drill Sergeant Emil Foley. Mayo is an excellent cadet, but a little cold around the heart, so Foley rides him mercilessly, sensing that the young man would be prime officer material if he weren't so self-involved. Zack's affair with a working girl is likewise compromised by his unwillingness to give of himself.\n\nRated R · Released 28 Jul 1982 · United States of America · Language: English · 124 min\nStudio: Paramount Pictures, Lorimar Motion Pictures\n\nOn your server — Audio: English","releaseInfo":"1982","genres":["Drama","Romance","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"7.0","runtime":"124 min","cast":["Richard Gere","Debra Winger","Louis Gossett Jr.","David Keith","Robert Loggia","Lisa Blount","Lisa Eilbacher","Harold Sylvester"],"director":["Taylor Hackford"],"released":"1982-07-28T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"Life gave him nothing, except the courage to win...and a woman to love.","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Taylor Hackford","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/aAP9RYT7XxUiC2NZL9Hi2gEdxGB.jpg"},{"name":"Richard Gere","character":"Zack Mayo","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/i7wcBNmFldh2E4QInCvmv7CPSIR.jpg"},{"name":"Debra Winger","character":"Paula Pokrifki","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/iHZ2mZHEaNYFhEpnSguk043SKVE.jpg"},{"name":"Louis Gossett Jr.","character":"Sergeant Emil Foley","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/gNdTmckVFDz5M9k9zMiwCFb2cl9.jpg"},{"name":"David Keith","